WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.190
Customer keywords, a better page, and a strong Business Profile.

2
00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:08.040
This is the video for module two of the SEO course.

3
00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:15.750
Business owners often describe their products in their own language. Customers may use very different words.

4
00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:20.900
A caterer may say finger foods, while customers in Lagos type small chops.

5
00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:26.890
So first you find the customer's words, and decide which page answers each one.

6
00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:35.670
Then you rewrite a page so people and Google understand it, and you build a Google Business Profile that wins local searches.

7
00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:46.110
Write 5 to 10 plain seed words for what the business sells, in the customer's language, including Pidgin or local names if customers use them.

8
00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:58.200
Expand each seed with Google autocomplete, the People also ask boxes, and related searches at the bottom of the page. All free. Use an incognito tab.

9
00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:06.960
Search the best phrases and look at what ranks. Mark each one learn, compare, buy or visit. That is the search intent.

10
00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:14.890
Group phrases that mean the same thing. Small chops Lekki and small chops in Lekki Lagos belong together.

11
00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:22.820
Then give each group one page. Use the main keyword naturally in the title, a heading and the opening text.

12
00:01:23.170 --> 00:01:28.370
Repeating it everywhere is called keyword stuffing, and Google's spam policies forbid it.

13
00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:37.280
For example, Funke bakes celebration cakes in Ibadan. One evening, using only her phone, she writes her seed words.

14
00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:45.650
Autocomplete for birthday cake Ibadan shows birthday cake delivery Ibadan, and birthday cake price in Ibadan.

15
00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:56.500
In Google Trends, set to Nigeria, she compares cupcakes and cake parfait over 12 months. Parfait is rising, so she adds a parfait section.

16
00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:05.140
She groups 23 phrases into 5 topics, one page each. Now no two pages compete for the same search.

17
00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:19.210
Before, her page title said Home, Products. The main heading said Welcome. The address was page 2, and the photo was a 4 megabyte file called IMG 4432.

18
00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:33.620
After, the title says Birthday Cakes in Ibadan, Same-Day Delivery, then her business name. One main heading, called H1, with subheadings for designs, prices, delivery areas and how to order.

19
00:02:33.970 --> 00:02:49.010
The new address uses short words with hyphens, with a 301 redirect from the old one so old links still work. The photo gets a clear name, alt text describing it, and shrinks to about 200 kilobytes for phones.

20
00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:58.050
For most small businesses, the fastest SEO win is the Google Business Profile. It appears in Maps and the local pack.

21
00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:04.670
Google ranks local results on three things. Relevance: how well your profile matches the search.

22
00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:09.870
Distance: how far you are from the searcher. You cannot change this.

23
00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:16.510
Prominence: how well known you are, from reviews, links and articles across the web.

24
00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:30.430
For example, Aisha opens a hair salon in Garki, Abuja. She names the profile exactly as her signboard reads, with no extra keywords, and picks the specific category Hair salon.

25
00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:35.100
She adds her address, hours and 12 real photos.

26
00:03:36.350 --> 00:03:41.320
She verifies with a short video of the signboard, the street and her chairs inside.

27
00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:49.500
After each appointment she sends a short WhatsApp message with her review link. 18 customers leave reviews.

28
00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:55.210
She replies to every review, even a 3-star one about waiting time.

29
00:03:55.560 --> 00:04:04.260
Google forbids fake reviews, paying for reviews, and asking only happy customers. Breaking these rules can get a profile suspended.

30
00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:22.130
To remember. Start from the customer's words. Give each group one page. Write a unique title, one H1 and a short address. Keep your name, address and phone identical on every site. And ask every customer for a review, then reply to all of them.

31
00:04:23.380 --> 00:04:33.200
Now build your keyword map, rewrite one page, and claim and complete a Business Profile. Then send a polite review request to 5 recent customers.

32
00:04:33.550 --> 00:04:35.490
Continue with the lessons below.
